proof.text:
Take $W=k^d$, let $ho_R(e)$ be the diagonal matrix with entries $e^{
u_j}$, and put $a=b_0\circ v$. Each entry is a Laurent monomial and $e^{
u_j}$ is a unit, so these matrices define a group-scheme homomorphism $E	o\operatorname{GL}(W)$. The homogeneous identity gives $b(e\cdot x)=ho_R(e)b(x)$ for every commutative $k$-algebra $R$; setting $x=v(w)$ proves $e\cdot a_R(w)=a_R(ho_R(e)w)$. The corresponding coaction is $c(e_j)=e_j\otimes t^{
u_j}$; its two identities follow from $\Delta(t^{
u_j})=t^{
u_j}\otimes t^{
u_j}$ and $\epsilon(t^{
u_j})=1$. In characteristic zero the matrix identities in step 3 give the same coaction identities. Empty matrices and empty coordinate lists give the constructions for $d=0$; for $s=0$ every Laurent monomial is $1$.
